%% DM26-0670

%% The core's own restarts, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/core-restarts.md "Step 5, the ticket" and "3 in detail"). The bootstrap services ask cert-issuer on their token alone, and a request not
%% admitted by the floor state is held. What opens an entry is an absence and time, or the credentials agent's own ticket, for its own pod.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Old as Credentials agent, outgoing
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant CI as cert-issuer (gate, floor state, record)
    participant Init as polar-init,<br/>a bootstrap service's pod
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant CA as Credentials agent, running

    alt a planned restart of the credentials agent: it hands over
        Old->>Bk: its drain begins (PrepareShutdown): a SuccessorTicket on cert-issuer-successor-tickets
        Bk->>CI: published_by the credentials agent, or it is not taken
        CI->>CI: bind it to the pod UID of the last client certificate it signed for the credentials agent
        CI->>CI: the ticket is an entry in the record, so a restarted cert-issuer reads it back
        Old->>Old: finishes its drain, and the pod<br/>restarts in place: the same UID
        Init->>CI: the successor's token-only requests, its client certificate and its custodian's
        CI->>CI: the token bound to that UID, once for each type, within five minutes
        CI->>Att: attestation-instance-requests, for that pod
        alt Genuine, or it could not ask
            CI-->>Init: signed, recorded with the path Ticketed, and unattested if it could not ask
        else NotGenuine
            CI->>CI: the ticket's use is given back
            CI-->>Init: refused
        end
    else a crash, a pod deleted or evicted, or a ticket spent or expired: no ticket admits it
        Init->>CI: the token-only request
        CI->>CI: held, until the floor state opens the entry
        Note over CI: The credentials agent present means heard within 60 s (PRESENCE_BOUND). Unheard while Cassini<br/>holds opens its entry alone (CredentialsAgentOnly). A fresh cluster, or both gone, opens every entry (All).
        CI->>Att: attestation-instance-requests, once it is open
        CI-->>Init: signed, or refused, as above
    else the observer or Cassini restarts, and the credentials agent is up: it vouches
        Init->>CI: the token-only request, for a bootstrap identity the floor state does not admit
        CI->>CI: held
        alt over Cassini, while its session holds
            CI->>Bk: offer it on cert-issuer-held-requests
            Bk->>CA: taken only from cert-issuer's identity
            CA->>CA: the rules: a bootstrap service,<br/>not its own successor, bound to a pod,<br/>client or server, the attestation agent<br/>asked, then the renewal rule
            CA->>Bk: the answer, on cert-issuer-held-replies
            Bk->>CI: published_by the credentials agent, or it is not taken
        else over mTLS, while its Cassini session is lost (Cassini itself restarting)
            CA->>CI: list /internal/held, on a timer: its asking is also its presence
            CA->>CI: its answer, there
        end
        alt vouched
            CI-->>Init: signed, recorded with the path Vouched
        else refused
            CI-->>Init: refused
        end
        Note over CI,CA: A Cassini restart so completes with only cert-issuer and the credentials agent up. A request offered again is given its answer again.
    end
